+# P3 · Terrain, curricula and the v1.0 baseline: test & tinker guide
+
+Companion to the P3 code, in the format of `TEST_AND_TINKER_P2.md`. **P3.1 (curriculum training) is implemented**: it
+was checked on CPU here and is described in full (section 4). **P3.2 to P3.4 are planned**: sections 5 to 7 say what
+each part will change, file by file, and why. They get the same full treatment when we implement them, each on top
+of the previous one, as with P1 and P2.
+
+Each part section covers:
+- what the code does and why;
+- the commands;
+- what to read in `go2_metrics.py` and TensorBoard, and how to interpret it;
+- the knobs;
+- symptoms and fixes;
+- a "done when" check.
+
+Reference tables are at the end.
+
+Contents
+1. Files and install
+2. Change map: what each part modifies, file by file (P3.1 done, P3.2 to P3.4 planned)
+3. Workflow and conventions (base command, run names, knobs, evaluation worlds, comparing, TensorBoard, visual checks)
+4. P3.1 Curriculum training: terrain tiles, terrain curriculum, command curriculum, slopes up to 25°
+5. P3.2 Foot slip from ground truth, and the foot-slip penalty decision (plan)
+6. P3.3 Privileged observations for the critic and a teacher (plan)
+7. P3.4 Baseline v1.0: final run, config card, checked export, harness report, git tag (plan)
+8. Reference: configuration keys and constants
+9. Reference: metrics glossary (P3)
+10. Troubleshooting
+11. Sources
