+## 5. P3.2 Foot slip from ground truth, and the foot-slip penalty decision (plan)
+
+### 5.1 Goal
+1. The harness measures **each foot's stance slip from simulation ground truth**, correctly on slopes and terrain.
+2. With that measurement, decide whether to train with a **generic foot-slip penalty** (Isaac Lab Spot
+   `foot_slip_penalty`), and record the decision and its evidence in the config card (P3.4).
+
+### 5.2 What is wrong with today's slip metric on terrain
+`m_slip()` takes the contact point's velocity (foot-sphere centre + ω × r, r = (0, 0, −R)) and keeps its horizontal
+part, averaged over the four feet. That is exact on flat ground, but on terrain it has four problems:
+- On a slope the foot slides along the surface. Its horizontal speed is the slip × cos θ (−6 % at 20°, −9 % at 25°).
+- The contact point is not under the sphere centre any more but along −n (n = ground normal).
+- A foot sinking into the soft contact moves along n, which partly shows up as horizontal speed on a slope.
+- The mean over feet hides which leg slips. I would expect the front feet to slip more facing downhill and the hind feet
+  facing uphill; per-foot numbers will tell.
+
+### 5.3 What will change, per file
+- **`go2_metrics.py`**
+  - The ground normal under each foot from `go2_terrain` (n = (−∂h/∂x, −∂h/∂y, 1) normalized; flat: (0, 0, 1)).
+  - Contact point = centre − R·n. Its velocity v_cp = v_centre + ω × (−R n). Tangential slip v_t = v_cp − (v_cp·n) n.
+  - Stance = foot force > 3 N, as now; the first sample of each stance is dropped, as now.
+  - New table "Foot slip per foot", per foot (FL, FR, RL, RR):
+    - `slip_v` [cm/s]: mean tangential speed in stance;
+    - `slip_d` [cm/stance]: tangential distance per complete stance;
+    - `slip_share` [%]: share of stance time above 2 cm/s.
+  - The existing `slip_v` / `slip_d` / `slip_ratio` become the tangential mean over feet. On flat ground n = (0, 0, 1)
+    and nothing changes, so flat CSVs stay comparable.
+  - Check: Genesis' own contact normals (`robot.get_contacts()`) against the lookup's normals on a few tiles.
+- **`go2_env.py`**
+  - `self.foot_slip` [N, 4]: contact-gated stance slip speed per foot, every policy step (also for P3.3).
+  - `_reward_foot_slip()`: Σ over feet of 1[|F| > `contact_force_threshold`] · |v_foot,xy|. That is Spot's form
+    (Isaac Lab `foot_slip_penalty`: planar world-frame velocity of the foot bodies, contact from the net force above
+    1 N; Isaac Lab's generic `feet_slide` computes the same).
+  - Option `reward_cfg["foot_slip_mode"]`: `"xy"` (Spot, default) or `"tangent"` (the harness quantity).
+- **`go2_train.py`**: `--foot-slip [W]`, `FOOT_SLIP_WEIGHT`.
+  - Spot uses −0.5 next to tracking 5 + 5 = 10; at our 1.5 + 0.75 = 2.25 that is −0.11. So W = 0.1 when given without
+    a value.
+  - It is negative, so the P1 penalty curriculum ramps it (×0.3 → 1 over 400 iterations).
+- **`go2_compare.py`**: `--preset slip` (per-foot slip, `slip_share`, `lin_err`, `through`, `CoT`).
+- **`go2_feet_plot.py`**: tangential speed on terrain recordings.
+
+### 5.4 The decision experiment
+```bash
+python go2_train.py -e go2-p32 $BASE --terrain --cmd-curriculum                    # = go2-p31, re-measured
+python go2_train.py -e go2-p32-slip $BASE --terrain --cmd-curriculum --foot-slip   # + penalty (2 seeds each)
+for R in go2-p32 go2-p32-slip; do
+    python go2_metrics.py -e $R --ckpt $CKPT; python go2_metrics.py -e $R --ckpt $CKPT --terrain grid
+    for S in 15 -15 25 -25; do python go2_metrics.py -e $R --ckpt $CKPT --slope $S; done
+done
+```
+A proposed rule (to agree on before looking at the numbers): keep the penalty if per-foot slip drops clearly on slopes
+and the grid (≥ 30 %, on both seeds), with `lin_err` within noise, `through` not lower on any type, and CoT not more
+than ~5 % higher. Record the decision either way, with the numbers.
+
+### 5.5 Done when
+- Per-foot tangential slip exists in the harness (flat values unchanged).
+- The A/B decision is taken with numbers on 2 seeds.
+- The decision is written in the config card: on/off, weight, contact threshold, xy or tangent, evidence.
