+## 6. P3.3 Privileged observations for the critic and a teacher (plan)
+
+### 6.1 Goal
+A privileged observation vector that the **critic** reads (asymmetric actor-critic), and that a **teacher** policy
+could read (for a later student/teacher distillation). The deployed actor stays blind.
+
+Why the critic:
+- PPO's advantages come from the critic's value estimates.
+- A critic that sees the true base velocity, the friction and the contacts predicts returns better under domain
+  randomization and terrain, so the gradient is less noisy.
+- The actor is unchanged, so nothing changes on the robot.
+
+legged_gym has the same hook (`num_privileged_obs`, `privileged_obs_buf`). Lee et al. 2020 trained a privileged
+teacher and distilled it into a proprioceptive student.
+
+### 6.2 The vector
+All entries noise-free, scaled to about ±1. The env already draws and stores the DR values (`friction`, `added_mass`,
+`com_shift`, `motor_strength`, P1.2).
+
+| Entry | Size | Scale | Mirror (for `--symmetry`) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| base linear velocity (body frame) | 3 | × 2.0 (`obs_scales.lin_vel`) | (vx, −vy, vz) |
+| contact friction μ | 1 | (μ − 0.8) / 0.4 | unchanged |
+| added base mass | 1 | / 2 kg | unchanged |
+| base CoM shift | 3 | / 0.05 m | (x, −y, z) |
+| motor strength per joint | 12 | (k − 1) / 0.1 | legs swapped FL↔FR, RL↔RR, no sign change |
+| foot contact force (world) | 4 × 3 | / 100 N, clipped | feet swapped, y component negated |
+| foot slip (P3.2) | 4 | / 0.2 m/s | feet swapped |
+| optional: ground height under each foot, relative to the base | 4 | / 0.3 m | feet swapped |
+| optional (teacher on terrain): height scan, legged_gym's 17 × 11 points | 187 | / 0.3 m | grid mirrored in y |
+
+### 6.3 What will change, per file
+- **`go2_env.py`**: `obs_cfg["privileged"]`: the list of entries (none by default). `_update_observation()` builds
+  `self.privileged_buf`, and the env returns `TensorDict({"policy": ..., "privileged": ...})`.
+- **`go2_train.py`**: `--privileged critic` / `teacher` sets rsl_rl 5.5.1's `obs_groups`:
+  - critic: `{"actor": ["policy"], "critic": ["policy", "privileged"]}`;
+  - teacher: the actor gets `["policy", "privileged"]` too.
+
+  (rsl_rl's distillation uses the sets `"student"` / `"teacher"`.)
+- **`go2_symmetry.py`**: the mirror of each entry (table above). `python go2_symmetry.py --privileged` checks it with
+  the mirrored-rollout test.
+- **`go2_export.py`**: unchanged for critic runs (the export takes the actor, which reads `policy` only). It refuses
+  teacher runs, whose actor needs privileged inputs.
+- **`go2_metrics.py`**: nothing for critic runs. Teacher runs: the harness passes the privileged group (Genesis
+  computes it anyway).
+
+### 6.4 Experiment and done when
+```bash
+python go2_train.py -e go2-p33 $BASE --terrain --cmd-curriculum <P3.2 decision> --privileged critic   # 2 seeds
+```
+Compare with `go2-p32` (same flags without `--privileged`):
+- TensorBoard: `Train/mean_reward`, `Curriculum/terrain_level` over iterations (faster, or higher at the end?), and
+  the value loss;
+- harness: flat, grid, slopes.
+
+**Done when**: the privileged-critic run learns at least as fast and ends at least as high on 2 seeds, the mirror
+check passes with the new group, and the export is unchanged. Keep it for v1.0 only if it helps.
+
