+## 7. P3.4 Baseline v1.0: final run, config card, checked export, harness report, git tag (plan)
+
+### 7.1 Goal
+Freeze one policy as **Baseline v1.0**, the reference for everything after P3:
+- the final run, with the P3.1–P3.3 choices;
+- a one-page config card;
+- an export checked against the training model;
+- the harness report;
+- a git tag.
+
+### 7.2 The final run
+```bash
+V1FLAGS="--terrain --cmd-curriculum <P3.2 decision> <P3.3 decision> --set env.reset_forward=True"
+python go2_train.py -e go2-v1.0 $BASE $V1FLAGS            # + -s2 and -s3 for the thesis
+```
+`reset_forward=True` removes the reset kick on flat tiles too (4.1.8). The freeze is the moment to take it, since it
+ends bit-identity with P2 anyway.
+
+### 7.3 What will change, per file
+- **`go2_card.py`** (new): `python go2_card.py -e go2-v1.0 --ckpt N` writes `logs/go2-v1.0/CONFIG_CARD.md`, one page:
+  - identity: run, checkpoint, date, git commit and dirty flag (`logs/<exp>/git/`), Genesis / rsl_rl / torch versions;
+  - training: flags, iterations, envs, seed;
+  - world: DR ranges, the `[S2R]` contact model, terrain (types, levels, where the curriculum ended per type), command
+    ranges reached;
+  - observation and action layout; rewards (weights, sources); network;
+  - headline results from the harness report (flat 0.5 m/s, grid frontiers, ±20° slopes, gate);
+  - export: files, sha256, max error of each check;
+  - decisions: P3.2 slip penalty, P3.3 privileged critic, `reset_forward`, with one line of evidence each.
+- **`go2_export.py`**: `--onnx` also writes `policy.onnx` (rsl_rl 5.5.1 `export_policy_to_onnx`, opset 18).
+  - Checked with onnxruntime against the training policy, as the TorchScript check already does. Two input sets:
+    100 random observations, and observations recorded by `go2_metrics.py` (a real state distribution).
+  - sha256 of both files go into `deploy_cfg["source"]`.
+  - Recurrent policies: check rsl_rl's ONNX inputs and outputs for the hidden state before relying on it.
+- **`go2_report.py`** (new): runs the standard set and collects `logs/<exp>/report/`:
+  - flat nominal, flat DR;
+  - own tiles, unseen tiles;
+  - slopes ±10 / ±20 / ±25;
+  - optionally the unitree_mujoco gate suite.
+
+  Output: one summary table and the PNGs. The same command then measures every later candidate against v1.0.
+- **`runs.md`**: the v1.0 row.
+
+### 7.4 Git tag and artifacts
+```bash
+git add -A && git commit -m "Baseline v1.0"          # the code that trained go2-v1.0
+git tag -a baseline-v1.0 -m "Baseline v1.0: go2-v1.0 ckpt N (CONFIG_CARD.md)"
+git push origin main baseline-v1.0
+gh release create baseline-v1.0 logs/go2-v1.0/exported/policy.pt logs/go2-v1.0/exported/policy.onnx \
+    logs/go2-v1.0/exported/deploy_cfg.json logs/go2-v1.0/CONFIG_CARD.md logs/go2-v1.0/terrain.npz \
+    --notes-file logs/go2-v1.0/CONFIG_CARD.md
+```
+Your `.gitignore` excludes `logs/`, `*.pt` and `*.onnx`, so the tag holds the code only. The release holds the
+policy, its config and its grid.
+
+### 7.5 Done when
+The card, the checked export (TorchScript and ONNX), the report and the tag exist and point to each other: commit
+hash in the card, card in the release, release on the tag.
